From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mvx: include linux/vmalloc.h explicitly

Building against 7.2 fails with:

  if/mvx_mmu.c:781:11: error: assignment to 'struct mvx_mmu_pages *' from
  'int' makes pointer from integer without a cast [-Wint-conversion]
      pages = vmalloc(sizeof(*pages) + sizeof(phys_addr_t) * capacity);

vmalloc() is implicitly declared, so the compiler assumes it returns int.
mvx_mmu.c never included <linux/vmalloc.h>; it had been getting the
declaration transitively through another header, and that indirect include
is gone in this kernel. Include it directly rather than relying on a
transitive path that upstream is free to remove again.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree]
The CIX P1 VPU driver is a vendor drop with no upstream submission path;
sent downstream only.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
--- a/driver/if/mvx_mmu.c
+++ b/driver/if/mvx_mmu.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/list.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include "mvx_mmu.h"
 #include "mvx_log_group.h"
 
